But what if `r->hs` is something else? The resampler selection:
```c
if      (r->hs == 1 && r->vs == 1) r->resample = resample_row_1;
else if (r->hs == 1 && r->vs == 2) r->resample = stbi__resample_row_v_2;
else if (r->hs == 2 && r->vs == 1) r->resample = stbi__resample_row_h_2;
else if (r->hs == 2 && r->vs == 2) r->resample = z->resample_row_hv_2_kernel;
else                               r->resample = stbi__resample_row_generic;
```

The `stbi__resample_row_generic` writes `w*hs` bytes. With `hs` up to 4 (since h_max up to 4, h up to 1, ratio up to 4). `w_lores = (img_x + hs-1)/hs`. So `w_lores * hs <= img_x + hs - 1`. With `hs=4`, that's `img_x + 3`. linebuf is `img_x + 3`. OK, fits exactly.

